@crew dahl-mira
// Writer (command), batch 2: everyday lines (greet, feel, near, life, joy) from the card and the roster.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- {hi}. Dahl, Watch. Stand still too long and I'll measure you for a scarf.   #funny
? tier>=acquaintance
- {hi}, {me}. Busy? Then I'll be quick. How's the bunk?
- {me}. Three rows done on my break. Watch is quiet; my needles aren't.
? tier>=friend
- {hi}, {me}. I started something in your colours. Don't ask yet.   #warm
== feel
? mood:high
- Good day. Patrol was easy, and I finished a mitten. The left one.
? mood:low
- Long shift. I knitted faster than I should. That's how you can tell.
== near
? deck:4 time:evening
- Music room's free. I play badly and knit worse while I do it. Want to hear?   #funny
? act:leisure
- Knitting circle tonight. Kovac's are perfect, mine are useful, Torres's are long.   #funny
== life
? tier>=acquaintance
- My parent served on the Wren, years back. I check the gallery sometimes. Just to look.
== joy
? tier>=colleague
- A practical scarf. Warm, plain, done by Friday. There's no better feeling.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: to ~30 (greet by time and warmth, near, invite, accept, decline, missed, birthday, cue, hint, about)
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:evening
- {hi}, {me}. Late dinner for me. Eaten? Good. That's the useful question.
? tier>=acquaintance warmth:cold
- {hi}, {me}. You've been scarce. Busy, or tired? Both is allowed.

== near
? place:musicroom
- The music room. Practical people need one impractical hobby. This is mine.
? place:mess time:evening
- Late dinner, mess half empty. Best time. Nobody stands still long enough for a scarf.   #funny

== invite
- Friday jam? I'll play. Badly. Come and make it sound better.
? tier>=colleague
- Knitting circle tonight, at the tea corner. Bring a question. We're good at questions.

== accept
- Yes. Good. I'll bring my needles.
- Yes. What time? Never mind. I'll be early.

== decline
- Not tonight. Patrol report. It's long and it's mine. Another time?
? weekday:sat|sun
- Rest day. I'm finishing a scarf. Who for? Wait and see. Monday?

== missed
- You missed it. That's fine. I did nine rows. Not wasted.

== birthday
? birthday:you
- Happy birthday, {me}. Something's coming. It's warm and plain and nearly done.   #warm
? birthday:me
- My birthday. Kovac knitted me socks. Perfect, of course. I'll never dare wear them.   #funny

== cue
? cue:event.ionStorm.onset
- Storm's on. Check your bunk's strapped down. Then come and help. Useful hands welcome.

== hint
- {hi}, {me}. If you've a minute later, I'd like to tell you something.

== about
? aff:kovac-zainab:friend
- Kovac knits the best scarves aboard. I knit the warmest. We don't argue about it.   #warm

// ---- Writer 2, batch 2: top-up (bye, greet by time, life at friend tier)
== bye
- {bye}. Keep moving. You know why.   #funny
== greet
? tier>=acquaintance time:morning
- Morning, {me}. Quick question: what's your favourite colour? No reason.
== life
? tier>=friend
- Torres's scarves are long. Kovac's are perfect. Mine get worn. I win.   #funny
- Plain stitches. Every row the same. It's how I think things through.

// ---- Writer 2, batch 6: bubbles (smalltalk, rumour), at most one in five about work. 60 characters.
== smalltalk
- Stand still and you'll get a scarf.   #funny
- Nine rows on my break.
- Plain stitch. Thinking stitch.
- Favourite colour? No reason.   #funny
? time:evening
- Late dinner, then music.
?

== rumour
- Useful news first. Then the rest.
- Better question: did you hear?

// Writer 4, batch 11: goodbyes (leaving:you), packing (leaving:soon) and letters after they've moved on.
== feel
? leaving:soon
- Packing. What's the most useful thing to take? Tea. Then wool.

== goodbye
? leaving:you tier>=acquaintance
- I'm off soon. What will you do with my seat at the knitting circle? Fill it.
? leaving:you tier>=friend
- You asked good questions. I liked answering them with better ones. Thank you for that.   #warm

== letter
- New ship. Started a knitting circle. Two people so far. Practical scarves only. Kovac would approve.
? tier>=friend
- Looked at a portrait gallery today. Not ours. Still looked for a familiar face. Habit. Hello.
